WEBVTT

00:00:03.494 --> 00:00:08.379
<v><b>Host:</b></v> OK, Eddie, first question for 100 dollars:

00:00:08.963 --> 00:00:15.240
A wolf can make a louder noise than a lion. True or false?

00:00:17.623 --> 00:00:20.845
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> A wolf can make a louder noise than a lion.

00:00:25.444 --> 00:00:28.334
Uh, false I’d say.

00:00:29.919 --> 00:00:30.771
<v><b>Host:</b></v> Correct!

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:36.413
Wolves make a sound of approximately 90 decibels when they howl,

00:00:36.606 --> 00:00:41.363
whereas a lion’s roar is about 114 decibels.

00:00:42.841 --> 00:00:45.360
Now, for 200 dollars:

00:00:45.782 --> 00:00:49.875
Stonehenge, the stone circle in southwest England,

00:00:49.985 --> 00:00:56.128
is older than the Pyramids of Giza in Egypt. True or false?

00:00:56.336 --> 00:00:58.827
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Uh, I think it’s true.

00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:03.335
<v><b>Host:</b></v> Correct! It’s true.

00:01:03.638 --> 00:01:08.545
The construction of Stonehenge began about 5,000 years ago,

00:01:08.866 --> 00:01:14.780
but the construction of the pyramids actually began about 450 years later.

00:01:15.751 --> 00:01:23.824
Next, for 400 dollars, the island of Cuba is bigger than the island of Iceland.

00:01:24.673 --> 00:01:32.585
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> I think it’s true. Cuba is much bigger than people think. So yes, it’s true.

00:01:34.321 --> 00:01:37.157
<v><b>Host:</b></v> Correct, though it’s not by much.

00:01:37.604 --> 00:01:48.004
Cuba is 42,803 square miles and Iceland is 39,768 square miles.

00:01:49.117 --> 00:01:57.257
Next, for 800 dollars: Ireland is wetter than Brazil. True or false?

00:01:58.227 --> 00:02:00.710
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Ireland is wetter than Brazil.

00:02:01.192 --> 00:02:05.475
Uh, false. I know it rains a lot in Ireland,

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:10.247
but Brazil has rainforests, so I’m sure it rains more there.

00:02:12.654 --> 00:02:13.891
<v><b>Host:</b></v> Correct!

00:02:16.151 --> 00:02:24.214
The average rainfall in Brazil is 69 inches a year, and in Ireland it’s only 44.

00:02:24.787 --> 00:02:28.213
Well, I say <i>only</i>, but it’s still a lot!

00:02:28.649 --> 00:02:32.913
Good job, Eddie, that’s four correct answers so far.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.694
Next, for 1,600 dollars:

00:02:39.426 --> 00:02:46.457
a baby elephant is heavier than an adult panda. True or false?

00:02:47.173 --> 00:02:54.705
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Uh, true. No, uh, false. Uh, I’m not sure.

00:02:55.406 --> 00:02:57.328
<v><b>Host:</b></v> Do you want to call a friend?

00:02:57.353 --> 00:03:00.120
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> No, I think it’s true.

00:03:00.644 --> 00:03:03.212
I know baby pandas are tiny,

00:03:03.237 --> 00:03:06.894
and maybe even full-grown ones aren’t as heavy as we might think.

00:03:07.468 --> 00:03:09.078
I’m saying it’s true.

00:03:12.027 --> 00:03:12.969
<v><b>Host:</b></v> Correct!

00:03:13.188 --> 00:03:18.715
A newborn baby elephant can weigh as much as 264 pounds,

00:03:19.166 --> 00:03:24.307
but an adult panda never weighs more than 250 pounds. Huh!

00:03:25.345 --> 00:03:34.886
OK, for 3,200 dollars, life in New York is more expensive than life in Paris.

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:40.280
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Uh, true. I’m pretty sure New York is more expensive.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:42.753
<v><b>Host:</b></v> Correct!

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:50.049
New York is usually in the top five on the list of expensive cities to live in,

00:03:50.178 --> 00:03:52.900
along with Hong Kong and Singapore.

00:03:53.545 --> 00:03:59.256
Paris is still expensive, of course, but it’s a lot cheaper than New York right now.

00:04:00.115 --> 00:04:06.337
OK, Eddie, now question seven, for 6,400 dollars...

00:04:06.943 --> 00:04:13.265
The mountain K2 is more difficult to climb than Mount Kilimanjaro.

00:04:13.758 --> 00:04:15.539
True or false?

00:04:16.437 --> 00:04:22.213
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Uh, I think that’s true. I know K2 is incredibly dangerous.

00:04:23.387 --> 00:04:25.725
<v><b>Host:</b></v> Good job, Eddie.

00:04:27.211 --> 00:04:33.552
25% of the people who climb K2 die, usually on the way down,

00:04:33.694 --> 00:04:38.500
but fewer than 1% of the people who climb Kilimanjaro die.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:42.408
And finally, the last question.

00:04:42.969 --> 00:04:44.649
Be very careful, Eddie.

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:53.704
If you get it right, you win 12,800 dollars, but if you get it wrong, you get nothing.

00:04:54.256 --> 00:04:55.376
Are you ready?

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:57.155
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Yes, ready.

00:04:57.694 --> 00:05:01.570
<v><b>Host:</b></v> OK, for 12,800 dollars,

00:05:04.433 --> 00:05:09.207
white chocolate is better for you than milk chocolate.

00:05:10.036 --> 00:05:14.481
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Uh… uh…

00:05:14.674 --> 00:05:16.569
<v><b>Host:</b></v> I need your answer, Eddie.

00:05:16.787 --> 00:05:22.459
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> I think it’s true, but I’m not sure. I want to call a friend.

00:05:22.484 --> 00:05:26.404
<v><b>Host:</b></v> OK, Eddie. So, who do you want to call?

00:05:26.429 --> 00:05:28.630
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Uh, my dad, Brian.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.138
<v><b>Host:</b></v> OK then.

00:05:33.602 --> 00:05:35.491
Hello, is this Brian?

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:37.500
<v><b>Mia:</b></v> No, it’s Mia.

00:05:37.962 --> 00:05:42.197
<v><b>Host:</b></v> Uh, I’m calling from <i>Quiz Night</i>. Is Brian there?

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:46.549
<v><b>Mia:</b></v> Dad’s not here. I’m Eddie’s sister. I can help.

00:05:46.995 --> 00:05:49.803
<v><b>Host:</b></v> OK, Mia, Eddie needs some help.

00:05:50.178 --> 00:05:53.676
You have 30 seconds, Eddie. Here she is.

00:05:54.317 --> 00:05:57.440
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> OK… Hi, Mia, listen…

00:05:57.702 --> 00:05:58.716
<v><b>Mia:</b></v> Hi, Eddie.

00:05:59.051 --> 00:06:01.643
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> It’s the last question in the quiz.

00:06:01.829 --> 00:06:07.736
“White chocolate is better for you than milk chocolate.” I think it’s true.

00:06:08.357 --> 00:06:13.108
<v><b>Mia:</b></v> Uh, OK, I’m sure there’s more sugar in white chocolate. I think it’s false.

00:06:13.387 --> 00:06:21.337
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Um, I don’t think so. I think white chocolate is healthier.

00:06:21.585 --> 00:06:23.570
<v><b>Mia:</b></v> I’m right on this one, Eddie.

00:06:23.866 --> 00:06:30.308
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Um, OK... uh, really difficult, I can’t decide.

00:06:30.907 --> 00:06:32.737
<v><b>Host:</b></v> Time’s up, I’m afraid.

00:06:34.581 --> 00:06:38.877
OK, Eddie. So, true or false?

00:06:39.497 --> 00:06:45.987
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Uh, oh, I don’t know, I don’t think she’s right.

00:06:46.453 --> 00:06:47.969
I’m going to say true.

00:06:48.882 --> 00:06:50.226
<v><b>Host:</b></v> Final answer?

00:06:50.616 --> 00:06:52.905
<v><b>Eddie:</b></v> Final answer. True.

00:06:54.918 --> 00:06:59.041
<v><b>Host:</b></v> Aah. I’m sorry, Eddie, it’s false.

00:07:00.937 --> 00:07:06.543
In 100 grams of white chocolate, there are 59 grams of sugar;

00:07:06.715 --> 00:07:10.160
in milk chocolate, it’s 52 grams.

00:07:10.691 --> 00:07:18.230
Eddie, you had 6,400 dollars, but now you go home with… nothing.